The core implementation of the Coherence database web app has been built inside `/Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon` in Node ES modules (Node 20+) and PostgreSQL 17 SQL, together with [IMPLEMENTATION.md](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/IMPLEMENTATION.md).

### What Was Built

1. **PostgreSQL 17 Schema and Invariants (R6, R7, R8, R9, R11, R14):**
   - [001_schema.sql](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/migrations/001_schema.sql) defines all 22 data shapes (20 immutable business tables and 2 operational tables: `review_submissions` and attempt-keyed `review_drafts`), partial unique indexes (linear standing input chain, one start/end/superseded per attempt, one start per request, one sent carry per date, one pending submission per run), `object_name = 'objects/' || sha256`, and composite `(store_kind, sha256)` foreign keys binding engine versions and code-bearing artifacts strictly to `nusear_code`.
   - [002_invariants_and_triggers.sql](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/migrations/002_invariants_and_triggers.sql) enforces every invariant in PostgreSQL with `SET search_path = pg_catalog`: `ENABLE ALWAYS TRIGGER` blocking `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, and `TRUNCATE` under all replication settings; `SERIALIZABLE`-only single-row journal inserts with gapless `seq`, `prev_hash`, monotonic `recorded_at`, and recomputed SHA-256 over `coherence.canonical_json()` (verifying caller-provided values without overwriting them); `created_xid = pg_current_xact_id()` and deferred commitment triggers preventing late row additions; case/NFC twins and file-folder clash checks; entry-derived `Sent/` and `Overlay/` carry protection; session advisory lock checks bound to `(pg_backend_pid(), own_backend_start())`; and every R8 state transition guard.
   - [003_views_and_roles.sql](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/migrations/003_views_and_roles.sql) provides derived `coherence.run_stage(run_id, as_of_seq)` and `coherence.run_states`, `approvals_full_rows` / `approvals_current` / `approvals_bible_applied`, `standing_input_version_as_of`, and least-privilege `coherence_app`, `coherence_worker`, and `coherence_readonly` roles without table-lock privileges on business tables.
   - [pg-client.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/db/pg-client.mjs), [wire-pg.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/db/wire-pg.mjs), and [migrate.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/db/migrate.mjs) provide the PostgreSQL 17 connection layer (`pg` 8.13.1 when installed, with a built-in zero-dependency PG v3 wire fallback) and idempotent migration runner.

2. **The Two Separated Stores (R6.2, R6.6, R6.11, R9.7, R10.8, R14.1):**
   - [artifact-policy.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/storage/artifact-policy.mjs), [object-store.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/storage/object-store.mjs), and [stores.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/storage/stores.mjs) implement Nusear's code store (`nusear_code`) and the company's data store (`company_data`) with GCS (`ifGenerationMatch=0`), local filesystem, and in-memory backends, MD5 and CRC32C verification on both fresh uploads and existing objects, promotion strictly after `checksPassed: true`, separate review staging outside `objects/`, and path-plus-content refusal of code-bearing bytes in `company_data`.

3. **Command Layer and Journal Export / Rebuild (R4, R8, R9, R10):**
   - [authz.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/commands/authz.mjs), [commitments.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/commands/commitments.mjs), [command-layer.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/commands/command-layer.mjs), and [journal-export.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/commands/journal-export.mjs) implement actor and View-As enforcement, `command_key` and `request_sha256` idempotency, `expectedJournalSeq` optimistic concurrency, batched `unnest` writes, all R8 commands, NDJSON journal export, exact database rebuild verification, and independent `chain`, `commitments`, and `objects` checks.

4. **Extended Overlay Checker and Engine Worker (R5, R10):**
   - [coherence_overlay_check.py](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/python/coherence_overlay_check.py) extends Nusear's overlay check under Coherence's own `overlay._read()` to report `header_kind` (`v1`/`v2`) and `new_rows`.
   - [slot.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/worker/slot.mjs), [reconciler.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/worker/reconciler.mjs), [folder-builder.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/worker/folder-builder.mjs), [engine-runner.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/worker/engine-runner.mjs), and [worker.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/worker/worker.mjs) implement the advisory-lock running slot with out-of-transaction liveness checks, dead-attempt reconciliation, verified workspace materialization and post-step frozen-input re-hashing, UTF-8 / `America/New_York` step execution across all Emit modes, process-group kill on cancel / 15-minute timeout / slot loss, and non-stalling review submission processing.

5. **History Importer and Run Folder Comparator (R12, R13):**
   - [history-importer.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/importer/history-importer.mjs) implements manifest-first, read-only, idempotent, resumable imports for Phalanx and Clearpath with byte-for-byte folder rebuild proofs and SQLite parity counts.
   - [run-comparator.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/compare/run-comparator.mjs) compares inputs file by file first and supports `storage`, `replay`, `shadow`, `trial`, and `clearpath_vs_mac` comparison rules.

6. **Downstream Reader and Web Endpoints (R15, R16):**
   - [downstream-reader.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/readers/downstream-reader.mjs) reads only the newest finished, non-abandoned `app` or `company_import` run from the database and stores, matching `lib/coherence.mjs` and `lib/clearpath-feed.mjs` (HMAC verification, nonce replay guard, no-dollar 24-column `AGENT_BOOK_COLUMNS` filter).
   - [handlers.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/web/handlers.mjs), [router.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/web/router.mjs), and [drift-check.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/src/web/drift-check.mjs) provide all R16 server-side handlers (Inputs, Staging, Runs, Reviews, History "as of", Run journal, Approval key history over POST body to keep member data out of URL logs, Checks, scope-checked non-sandboxed Bundles, and review app drift checks).

7. **Tests (R18, R11):**
   - Six `node:test` suites under `tests/`: [01_schema_invariants.test.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/tests/01_schema_invariants.test.mjs), [02_commands_and_races.test.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/tests/02_commands_and_races.test.mjs), [03_stores_and_security.test.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/tests/03_stores_and_security.test.mjs), [04_worker_and_failures.test.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/tests/04_worker_and_failures.test.mjs), [05_import_compare_replay.test.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/tests/05_import_compare_replay.test.mjs), and [06_readers_and_web.test.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/tests/06_readers_and_web.test.mjs), supported by [test-db.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/tests/helpers/test-db.mjs) and [fixtures.mjs](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/tests/helpers/fixtures.mjs).

8. **Documentation:**
   - [IMPLEMENTATION.md](file:///Users/marcsmac/Code/coherence-db-neon/IMPLEMENTATION.md) maps every requirement (R1 to R19), lists design choices, records ambiguities and open items, details the verification order for a real PostgreSQL 17 server, and states plainly that all SQL, Node, Python, and test files are untested because commands could not be run in this session.
